  "copy": "<span class=\"dl\">MANILA:</span> Prime Minister Narendra Modi arrived in the Philippine capital on Monday for the 23rd India-ASEAN Summit and the 21st East Asia Summit, both on Tuesday. President Ferdinand Marcos Jr hosted a dinner for visiting leaders. Before it, Modi viewed the Laguna Copperplate Inscription, the oldest dated document found in the Philippines (around 900 CE), which records ancient links with India. The summits open under strain. ASEAN and China failed to finish a South China Sea code of conduct, though about 80% of the draft is agreed, and India restated its support for freedom of navigation. Indonesia’s President Prabowo Subianto apologised to Singapore and Malaysia over smoke from his country’s worst wildfires in 11 years. Whether Quad leaders will meet on the sidelines is still unclear.",
